{
  "skip": false,
  "summary": "Wires up server-side i18n locale fallbacks: registers the fallbacks/pluralization backends, defines a FallbackLocaleList (user locale -> site default -> :en), and forces the fallback chain to be loaded on each request via ensure_loaded!. It also correctly removes the previously-inert config.i18n.fallbacks = true declarations, which never had any effect. Logic is sound and matches the existing translate_accelerator caching/loading conventions; no correctness or security issues found.",
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "findings": [
    {
      "path": "config/initializers/i18n.rb",
      "line": 17,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "severity": "Important",
      "title": "No test coverage for the new fallback behavior",
      "body": "FallbackLocaleList#[] and #ensure_loaded! introduce the core fallback-order logic (user locale -> SiteSetting.default_locale -> :en) but no spec exercises it; a regression here (e.g. wrong fallback order, or SiteSetting.default_locale not being callable during early boot) would only surface as silently-missing translations in production rather than a failing test."
    }
  ]
